# The archive's folder, or the link the move out of the checkout left at its old place. Private; never committed.
/data
node_modules/
.env.local
# The static demo as npm run build:demo builds it (docs/demo.md): made again from the code on every build.
/dist-demo
# This installation's owner's own orders for their agents (AGENTS.md says to read it first), and Claude Code's link to it.
/AGENTS.local.md
/CLAUDE.local.md
# The modules (docs/modules.md): every folder under modules/ is ignored, so a private module cloned in, whose code is
# not this repository's, is never committed by accident; a module built in this repository is named below to track it.
/modules/*
!/modules/health/
!/modules/exercise/
!/modules/journal/
!/modules/rituals/
!/modules/friend-map/
!/modules/shopping/
!/modules/folder-history/
!/modules/inspirations/
# Rituals' per-installation files beside its code (modules/rituals/README.md): config/ (which Node, and where the
# store is), and a store kept beside the code when nothing names another place (never the captain's: his is in the
# archive's folder).
/modules/rituals/config/
/modules/rituals/data/
/modules/rituals/queue/
/modules/rituals/evidence/
/modules/rituals/logs/
/modules/rituals/.agent-work/
/devlog/
